    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d479">

                <pb facs="0674" n="574" xml:id="pg574"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">251.11 Insull, Samuel/365: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Greece</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >MacVeagh</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Athens</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1934-03-15T21:00:00+02:00">March 15, 1934—9
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received March 15—7:08 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>32. The Foreign Minister has just telephoned me that Insull has disappeared. He
                    further stated his belief that the fugitive must be hiding in Athens but I have
                    telegraphed Belgrade, Tirana, Sofia, Istanbul, Bucharest, Cairo, Beirut, Borne,
                    Jerusalem, Baghdad and Teheran. Mrs. Insull is here.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">MacVeagh</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
